codex
The claim domain is not finitely bounded: empty and singleton are separate, while `IntSeq` recursively represents every finite middle segment and `nonNegativeIS` constrains every element. The direct body mutation made the odd-branch proof stick on reverse-versus-ascending output, confirming that the theorem is sensitive to the actual executed closure. I’m now auditing the one proof-local operational bridge against bridge-free semantics and generating the exhaustive declaration/rule inventory.
