codex
The bridge audit found a real validation limitation, not a counterexample: bridge-free semantics proves ordinary concrete last-index executions, and the bridge preserves an observable `+ 10` continuation, but neither the exact symbolic claim domain nor the bridge’s broader `ValSeq` match domain has a bridge-free universal connection proof. The residual is precisely the missing `valSeqAt(...)=L` fact. I found no false intended-domain witness—the rule is the standard snoc/last lemma—so I’m recording this as an informal proof-extension boundary rather than calling it unsound.
apply patch
